# Frontend env — intentionally EMPTY for LAN / multi-user (remote) access. (PH-324)
#
# VITE_WS_URL and VITE_API_URL are deliberately NOT set here so the app uses
# HOST-RELATIVE URLs derived from window.location:
#   - HTTP: frontend/src/api/client.ts uses BASE="/api"; Vite proxies /api + /mcp
#           to the backend (see vite.config.ts).
#   - WS:   frontend/src/hooks/useWebSocket.ts connects straight to the backend origin
#           `${wsProtocol}//${window.location.hostname}:8000` when VITE_WS_URL is unset.
#           WS bypasses Vite entirely — vite-5's WS proxy can't forward the upgrade.
#
# Hard-coding localhost here breaks every remote/LAN client (the browser would
# open a WS to ITS OWN localhost). Leave empty. Set VITE_WS_URL only for prod
# (wss://) or a non-default backend port. See .env.example for production notes.
